  <h3 class="section-header">DEFINITIONS</h3>
  <p><strong>Volunteer</strong></p>
  <p>Section 553.101 of Title 29, Code of Federal Regulations defines a volunteer as "an individual who performs hours of service for a public agency for civic, charitable, or humanitarian reasons, without promise, expectation or receipt of compensation for services rendered... during such hours". In addition, an individual shall be considered a volunteer only where his/her services is offered freely and without pressure or coercion, direct or implied, from an employer.</p>
